   "subject": "Investigating invariance in multigroup SEM",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Hi lavaaners,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I have been working in a dataset comprised of cognitive and brain volumetric data. The aim is to compare two groups, cases and controls for a certain condition. The model include e latent variable in a MIMIC design.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">The design is similar to previous experiments that worked out fine, but in this particular case I do not get scalar invariance btw groups. The only thing that is different from previous experiments using other datasets is that now the cognitive data is a  z-scored sum of item scores, previously I used data from principal component analysis.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">How can I diagnose what indicators are involved in this?</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Here is a MWE with anonymized data:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">install.packages(&quot;RCurl&quot;)\r\nlibrary(RCurl)\r\n\r\ntest&lt;- read.csv(text = getURL(&quot;<a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lf-araujo/sempsychiatry/master/MWE.csv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lf-araujo/sempsychiatry/master/MWE.csv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427381643000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2lOBP_OOV9GG-n5rakxRqe\">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lf-araujo/sempsychiatry/master/MWE.csv</a>&quot;))\r\n\r\nsemModelMIMIC &lt;- &#39;\r\ng =~ A+B+C+ D\r\ng ~ E\r\n+   F\r\n+   G\r\n+   H\r\n+ I\r\n+ J\r\n+K\r\n+L\r\n&#39;\r\n\r\nfitInter &lt;- sem(semModelMIMIC, data = test,  estimator = &quot;MLM&quot;)\r\nfitmeasures(fitInter, c(&quot;df&quot;, &quot;rmsea&quot;, &quot;cfi&quot;, &quot;aic&quot;, &quot;chisq&quot;, &quot;pvalue&quot;))\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Gives me:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">      df    rmsea      cfi      aic    chisq   pvalue \r\n  26.000    0.000    1.000 7938.904   25.229    0.506\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">and:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">fitMulti &lt;- sem(semModelMIMIC, data = test,\r\n                estimator = &quot;MLM&quot;, group = &quot;M&quot;)\r\nfitmeasures(fitMulti, c(&quot;df&quot;, &quot;rmsea&quot;, &quot;cfi&quot;, &quot;aic&quot;, &quot;chisq&quot;, &quot;pvalue&quot;))\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Gives me:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">      df    rmsea      cfi      aic    chisq   pvalue \r\n  52.000    0.027    0.986 7698.828   56.956    0.296\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Then:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">measurementInvariance(semModelMIMIC, data = test, group = &quot;M&quot;,\r\n                      estimator = &quot;MLM&quot;)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Which gives me:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">Measurement invariance models:\r\n\r\nModel 1 : fit.configural\r\nModel 2 : fit.loadings\r\nModel 3 : fit.intercepts\r\nModel 4 : fit.means\r\n\r\nScaled Chi Square Difference Test (method = &quot;satorra.bentler.2001&quot;)\r\n\r\n               Df    AIC    BIC   Chisq Chisq diff Df diff Pr(&gt;Chisq)    \r\nfit.configural 52 7698.8 7840.2  56.956                                  \r\nfit.loadings   55 7694.7 7825.4  58.793      1.966       3  0.5794578    \r\nfit.intercepts 58 7723.4 7843.5  93.494     46.591       3  4.246e-10 ***\r\nfit.means      59 7733.7 7850.3 105.861     11.929       1  0.0005526 ***\r\n---\r\nSignif. codes:  0 ‘***’ 0.001 ‘**’ 0.01 ‘*’ 0.05 ‘.’ 0.1 ‘ ’ 1\r\n\r\nFit measures:\r\n\r\n               cfi.scaled rmsea.scaled cfi.scaled.delta rmsea.scaled.delta\r\nfit.configural      0.978        0.034               NA                 NA\r\nfit.loadings        0.981        0.030            0.003              0.003\r\nfit.intercepts      0.879        0.075            0.102              0.044\r\nfit.means           0.844        0.084            0.035              0.009\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Variable M is the factor with the condition. Variables A, B, C, D are the cognitive ones and the remainder are volumetric data.</p>\r\n<ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">It seems strange as the dataset is even a little larger (133,127) than previous experiments, but this time it is behaving differently. How to diagnose this further?</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Does the z-socored sum should be playing a role in this behaviour?</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Thank you,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">luis</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgbGF2YWFuZXJzLDxicj48YnI+PGJyPkkgaGF2ZSBiZWVuIHdvcmtpbmcgaW4gYSBkYXRhc2V0\r\nIGNvbXByaXNlZCBvZiBjb2duaXRpdmUgYW5kIGJyYWluIHZvbHVtZXRyaWMgZGF0YS4gVGhlIGFp\r\nbSBpcyB0byBjb21wYXJlIHR3byBncm91cHMsIGNhc2VzIGFuZCBjb250cm9scyBmb3IgYSBjZXJ